#### Company Description

Experian is a global data and technology company that drives opportunities for people and businesses around the world. We operate in diverse markets, such as financial services, healthcare, automotive, agribusiness, insurance, among others. Experian invests in people and in new advanced technologies to unleash the power of data. We have an amazing team of 25,200 employees in 32 countries.

Our uniqueness is valuing yours. Experian's culture, centered on people, inclusive and driven by purpose, is recognized by various awards — including World's Best Workplaces™ 2025 (Fortune Global Top 25) and Great Place To Work™ in 26 countries, among others. Check out Experian Life on social media or explore our careers site to understand why. Experian also takes pride in being an employer that promotes equal opportunity and affirmative action.

#### Job Description

- Perform the analysis and validation of documents, following the procedures, standards and guidelines established in the area's manuals and training;
- Ensure the quality and compliance of the analyses performed, meeting the standards defined by the operation;
- Keep up to date on processes, policies and workflows, ensuring the correct application of current rules;
- Take part in alignment meetings to track changes, procedure updates and relevant area communications;
- Take part in training and continuous development activities, contributing to the growth of technical and operational knowledge;
- Seek support from the team and leadership whenever necessary, ensuring questions are resolved and documents under analysis are handled appropriately;
- Contribute to process efficiency by meeting deadlines and paying attention to detail during activities.

#### Qualifications

- High school diploma;
- Knowledge of Microsoft Office;
- Attention to detail, critical thinking and analytical ability for document analysis and validation.
- Availability to work afternoon and night shifts;
- Availability for on-site work on a 5x2 schedule, with rotating days off, including Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.

#### Additional Information

Serasa Experian is much more than you imagine. With the purpose of creating a better future by expanding opportunities for people and businesses, in Brazil we are more than 4 thousand people working in various teams and specialties. Here, every skill and diversity complements each other, and you can work on what you love most. We are committed to building an inclusive culture and an environment where people can balance their careers with their personal commitments and interests, valuing well-being.

We are truly dedicated to being one of the best and most innovative companies to work for in the country, enabling amazing experiences and careers for our people. Our strong people-first approach is recognized externally through various market certifications: we were awarded by Great Place To Work™ in 24 countries and by the international Top Employers certification, in addition to being recognized as one of the best companies for young professionals and having a 4.6 rating on Glassdoor. Each recognition tells us we are on the right path, providing an increasingly better work environment for our talent.

Experian Careers - Creating a better tomorrow together

[Find out what its like to work for Experian by clicking here](https://www.experian.com/careers/)

