Here at ília, our positions are always open to everyone and are not restricted by gender, ethnicity, sexual orientation, social factors, physical or intellectual conditions (PWD), etc. We encourage applications from members of all minority groups!

#### **About ília**

We are specialists in technology, data and design, driving the digital transformation of major market players for over 10 years, in the financial, insurance and mobility sectors. With more than 450 professionals, we are present in Brazil and Europe, serving markets in Latin America, Europe and North America, developing high-quality digital products with a focus on business results. We are an innovative, creative team passionate about technology.

Certified by Great Place to Work for the 8th consecutive year, here at ília we believe people change the world, and we invest in them. Our awesome deliveries are made by people for people, after all, awesome people make awesome deliveries!

#Vempraília!

#### **About the position:**

We are looking for an HR Business Partner to act as a strategic partner to leaders, with a focus on technology teams. This person will be responsible for promoting a positive and strategic experience journey for our talent, connecting the pillars of people management to business objectives.

#### **Responsibilities:**

- Act consultatively with managers, supporting strategic decisions related to people management;
- Closely follow professionals (Ílians) allocated to projects, with both internal and external clients, acting as the HR point of contact;
- Lead and monitor the onboarding process for new employees, ensuring a welcoming experience aligned with the company culture;
- Support the structuring, implementation and maintenance of HR policies, programs and processes focused on development, culture and performance;
- Ensure the deployment of business and market strategy into actions for the Talent Management team;
- Support the creation and monitoring of PDIs (individual development plans) with leaders and employees;
- Manage the flows of recognition, merit, promotion and talent retention;
- Monitor and interpret strategic people indicators (e.g., turnover, absenteeism, eNPS, headcount) and propose corrective/preventive actions;
- Participate in performance cycles, including evaluations, feedback and calibrations;
- Support the offboarding flow, conducting offboarding interviews and proposing improvements based on insights;
- Promote a safe and positive environment, addressing sensitive topics of climate, engagement and career development.

#### **Requirements:**

- Completed higher education in Psychology, Business Administration, Human Resources or related fields;
- **Advanced or fluent English for daily communication with international teams.**
- Solid experience as an HRBP serving technology areas, ideally with prior experience in technology consultancies, professional services or outsourcing;
- Mastery of the dynamics and business model of consulting (such as talent allocation, _turnover_, margin/utilization and relationships with end clients);
- Knowledge of people management practices and trends geared toward agile and innovative environments;
- Experience structuring and executing onboarding, development and talent retention programs in fast-paced environments;
- Advanced analytical skills to monitor HR metrics and use data in strategic decision-making.
- Sharp business vision, with the ability to quickly understand client context and connect HR demands to the consultancy's business objectives;
- Clear communication, empathy, active listening and the ability to act as a trusted advisor (_trusted advisor_) to leaders.

#### **Benefits and Incentives:**

Hiring is under CLT (Brazilian labor regime) - 40 hours per week with flexible schedule, performed fully remotely. ília's benefits are designed to provide an AWESOME experience for each ílian; below you will find the benefits in summary. #vempraília

