#### **About the position:**

Support the operational and banking routines of the Treasury, ensuring organization, punctuality in scheduling financial commitments and process compliance through standardized routines (POPs) and daily checklists.

#### **Responsibilities:**

- **Payment Scheduling and Banking Routines:** Prepare and schedule payment batches in internet banking/banking platforms, strictly following the checklists for verifying bank details, amounts and due dates.
- **Daily Cash Flow Support:** Support the Treasury Specialist in the daily extraction of bank statements, bank balances and prior verification of executed vs. scheduled transactions.
- **Reconciliation and Receipts:** Extract, organize and file bank payment receipts in the respective repositories and support daily reconciliations of accounts payable and receivable.
- **Accounts Receivable and Collection:** Assist in monitoring the receivables portfolio, issuing and sending invoices/bills, and support inquiries on bank settlements.
- **Operational Discipline:** Comply with Standard Operating Procedures (POPs) and fill in routine visual controls (Jira/daily treasury closing checklists).

#### **Requirements:**

- Enrolled in Business Administration, Accounting, Economics, Production Engineering or related fields (from the 3rd semester onward);
- Intermediate/advanced Office suite (focus on Excel and Google Sheets for data organization and verification);
- Basic knowledge of financial mathematics, reconciliation and banking routines;
- High attention to detail, operational precision, organization and a sense of meeting deadlines (bank cut-off times);
- Good interpersonal communication and a transparent attitude to promptly flag deviations or operational questions.

#### **Differentials: (IF APPLICABLE)**

- Experience or knowledge of corporate ERP systems (SAP);
- Familiarity with task management tools (Jira/Trello/Workspace);
- Intermediate English.

#### **Benefits and Incentives:**

