If you enjoy Sales, artificial intelligence, accelerated growth, targets and a great work environment, take a look at this job!

We are looking for young talents who enjoy the art of persuasion and want to develop in sales to join our pre-sales team! As an SDR intern at Ask, you will make the first contact with the main hotels, resorts and inns in the country. Your main mission is to delight leads with our service chatbot and generate qualified meetings for our sales team.

**About us:**

Asksuite was voted the best chatbot platform in the world for the hospitality/tourism sector for 7 consecutive years. Our AI serves 24/7 through instant messaging, multilingual and across multiple service channels. Our omnichannel platform centralizes the human service of all of a hotel's channels on a single screen!

We have clients in more than 80 countries, we were voted the 1st best company to work for in SC by Great Place to Work and the 1st in the world by the Hotel Tech Awards, in the tech for tourism segment. Our team has approximately 150 talents and we are looking for someone eager to learn and grow together with us!

**What is expected from this position:**

- Map and prospect new business opportunities;

- Approach potential clients in a personalized way via phone, email, WhatsApp and social media;

- Lead the first stage of the sales process, generating interest in the solution and overcoming possible objections;

- Ensure the lead attends the demonstration meeting, conducted by a salesperson;

- Validate different prospecting channels;

- Constantly analyze the area's results and your own, seeking to improve the volume and quality of your performance.


**You will do very well if:**

- You are very communicative and enjoy talking and helping hoteliers across Brazil, especially by phone;

- You want to constantly evolve! Asksuite is constantly growing and you will learn a lot about business processes, advanced sales and negotiation techniques, market analysis, among other skills;

- You like targets and are motivated by challenges! The day-to-day of sales is much better if you enjoy the adrenaline of the end of the month;

- You are passionate about growing and developing! There is not much room here for complacent people, growth is the keyword! If you want to learn and improve every day, we are speaking the same language.


- Currently enrolled in higher education;

- Availability to work on-site in Florianópolis;

- Availability to intern 30 hours per week during **business hours;**

- Excellent verbal and written communication skills.


**It would be nice if you have (not mandatory):**

- Intermediate English and/or Spanish;

- Basic knowledge of the sales funnel;

- Experience in sales or commercial negotiation;

- Previous experience in startups.


**Why do people love being part of Asksuite?**

- Attractive stipend: R$2,000.00

- Internship allowance: R$150.00

- Education allowance: R$200.00

- In-company English and Spanish;

- Dental plan;

- Psychological assistance;

- Wellhub (formerly Gympass);

- Pet health plan (Guapeco);

- Birthday day off;

- Coffee, tea, cookies, yogurt and fruit;

- Being part of a new company in constant growth!

- Feedback culture and lots of development;

- No dress code!

- Flexible hours.


**Do you identify with this? Then hurry and register for our selection process!**

If you are not afraid of challenges, love solving problems, are always looking for ways to improve your performance, are focused on results, organization, and are committed to the activities you carry out, then this job is for you! We are looking for a Tech Leader to help develop our scalable platform, participating in all the structuring of projects and helping define technologies and methodologies!

**About us:**

Asksuite has been voted the best chatbot platform in the world for the hospitality/tourism industry for 7 consecutive years. Our AI serves 24/7 through instant messaging, multilingual and across multiple service channels. Our omnichannel platform centralizes human service from all of a hotel's channels on a single screen!

We have clients in more than 80 countries, were voted the 7th best company to work for in SC by Great Place to Work, and the 1st in the world by the Hotel Tech Awards in the technology for tourism segment. Our team has more than 100 talents in more than 7 countries, and we are looking for a person eager to learn and grow together with us.

**What is expected from this position?**

- Technical Leadership and Architecture: Design, guide, and make decisions about the architecture (front-end and back-end) of our systems, ensuring scalability, performance, security, and maintainability.

- Mentoring and People Development: Guide, mentor, and give technical feedback to the team's developers, encouraging continuous growth and the dissemination of knowledge.

- Hands-On Coding: Write high-quality code, develop complex features, perform automated testing, and actively participate in code reviews.

- Quality and Standards: Define and promote good development practices to maintain the quality of the team's deliveries.

- Facilitation and Unblocking: Identify and remove technical impediments, helping the team resolve complex engineering problems.

- Bridge with Business and Product: Work side by side with the Product and Design teams to translate business needs into clear technical requirements and realistic estimates.

- Process Evolution: Suggest and implement improvements to the software development lifecycle processes and agile methodologies.

**You will do very well if you:**

- Have solid practical experience as a Fullstack Developer and experience with technical leadership of software teams.

- Have a macro view of software architecture, design patterns, and highly available distributed SaaS systems.

- Are an exceptional problem solver, with the ability to break down complex problems and propose simple and efficient solutions.

- Have excellent communication skills and the ability to negotiate deadlines, priorities, and solutions with different stakeholders.

- Are driven by continuous learning, self-taught, and proactive in exploring new technologies, methodologies, and tools.

- Have a passion for developing people and building a strong, collaborative, results-focused technical culture.

- Are passionate about growth and want to develop. Here, people grow together with the company (and vice versa);

- Completed or ongoing higher education;

- At least 4 years of experience with Node.js;

- Experience as a Technical Lead;

- Basic English - for coding;

- Availability to work 40 hours per week.

**It would be nice if you have, but it is not required:**

- Experience with chatbots and/or startups;

- Experience with the following technologies:

  - Angular 2+;

  - Java (e.g., Play Framework/Spring);

  - NestJS

  - Relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL);

  - Use of cloud (e.g., AWS).
- Experience with automated testing.

**Why people love being part of Asksuite:**

**Our way of being:**

- We are a new company in constant growth;

- We have a culture of feedback and a lot of development;

- No dress code culture;

- We encourage language courses and training;

- We are in international expansion to more than 80 countries;

- We provide career development within the company;

- We are among the 10 best (small) companies to work for in SC by GPTW;

- We were considered the best company to work for in the world in the technology for hospitality segment, according to the Hotel Tech Awards.

**What we offer:**

- National health plan with no co-payment;

- Dental plan;

- Flash Benefits Card: R$1,250.00;

- Monthly education allowance: R$200.00;

- Wellhub (Gympass);

- Psychological assistance;

- Life insurance;

- Pet health plan;

- Relocation allowance (if necessary);

- Birthday day off;

- Flexible hours.

