#### Job Description

**Job description**

We are looking for a professional with a consultative sales profile and a strong prospecting focus, who will work on generating and qualifying business opportunities to support the growth of the Serasa Experian portfolio. This person will be responsible for identifying potential clients, developing strategic relationships and contributing to expanding commercial opportunities, working in partnership with Sales Executives and internal areas.

- Carry out active prospecting of new clients (outbound) through different channels, such as phone, email, LinkedIn and other market tools;
- Identify, qualify and develop business opportunities aligned with the company's strategy;
- Build and maintain relationships with decision-makers and influencers, understanding their business needs and challenges;
- Conduct initial presentations of Serasa Experian's solutions, sparking interest and generating opportunities for the sales team;
- Manage and track the prospecting pipeline, ensuring information is kept up to date in the CRM;
- Map companies, markets and strategic segments to identify new business opportunities;
- Schedule qualified meetings for Sales Executives, ensuring alignment with the ideal customer profile;
- Use performance indicators to guide commercial actions and maximize results;
- Work together with Marketing, Product and Sales to boost demand generation and opportunity conversion;
- Follow market trends, competitor movements and customer behavior, sharing relevant insights with internal teams;
- Contribute to achieving targets for opportunity generation, pipeline growth and area revenue.

#### Qualifications

**Requirements**

- Completed higher education in Business Administration, Commercial Management, Business Management, Management Processes, Economics and related fields;
- Prior experience in sales prospecting, Inside Sales, SDR, BDR or related areas;
- Experience with active prospecting and lead qualification in a B2B environment;
- Excellent verbal and written communication, with the ability to adapt to different types of interlocutors;
- Analytical profile for interpreting data, indicators and prioritizing opportunities;
- Organization and discipline for managing pipeline and commercial activities;
- Proactivity, resilience and a strong focus on results;
- Experience with CRM, preferably Salesforce;
- Intermediate Excel skills;
- Ability to work collaboratively with different areas and stakeholders.

**Differentials:**

- Experience in technology, data, financial services or B2B solutions companies;
- Knowledge of consultative sales methodologies;
- Familiarity with prospecting and sales intelligence tools, such as Sales Navigator, Apollo, RocketReach or similar;
- Experience in high-performance environments and sales targets.

#### Additional Information

Serasa Experian is much more than you imagine. With the purpose of creating a better future, expanding opportunities for people and businesses, in Brazil we are more than 4 thousand people working in various teams and specialties. Here, every knowledge and diversity complements each other, and you can work on what you love most. We are committed to building an inclusive culture and an environment where people can balance their career with their personal commitments and interests, valuing well-being.

We are dedicated to being one of the best and most innovative companies to work for in the country, enabling amazing experiences and careers for our people. Our strong people-first approach is recognized externally through various market certifications: we were awarded by Great Place To Work™ in 24 countries and the international Top Employers certification, in addition to being recognized as one of the best companies for young professionals and having a 4.6 rating on Glassdoor. Each recognition tells us we are on the right path, providing an increasingly better work environment for our talent.

